phase P3
title Suite foundations
description
    **Class:** not readily verifiable.

    **Kind:** verification-suite.

    **Goal:** the suite's foundations, shared by every area: a new, clean conformance suite at production quality in
    `packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/`, run through one Port against round 14 and, area by area, production; the 
    Spec,
    runner, coverage gate, one verdict form and the static-case surface. All Tasks here are done.

    **Verified by:** the Tasks' acceptance; the suite green on round 14, null-red and falsify clean at each Task's 
    close.

    **One iteration:** one Task: build it, run it on round 14 and the null runtime, run its mutants, review, gather
    findings by root cause.

    **Exit criteria:** every Task here is done (the area phases build on them); the foundations' own mutants are killed.

    **False pass:** agreeing with the old suite because it was copied, weaknesses included.

    **Caught by:** each area's audit, whose auditor writes its own mutants from the Specs.

    **Gates:** falsify (`packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/`); `nub run check`, which rejects a planted lint violation.

    **Failure limit:** 2.

    **Stops:** a guarantee change (a Spec Invariant added, dropped or changed); a guarantee that can't be met.

    **User's read:** the suite layout (round 1), each Spec revision, each changed expected result with its reason.

    **Draws from:**

    - skill:policy-verification (prove a suite; the coverage record);
    - skill:policy-testing (audit a suite; scenarios that enforce each Invariant written first);
    - skill:to-spec for the suite's own Spec;
    - skill:policy-convergence at the threshold; skill:review at the cadence; skill:check-benchmark on speed numbers.
tasks
    T4
        title       The suite's own Spec, Conformance.spec
        status      done
        priority    high
        description
            Write `packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/Conformance.spec` with skill:to-spec, next to
            the suite (README item 7):

            - the Port exposes no runtime internals and any runtime implementing it gets the same
              verdicts;
            - expected results come from a cited Spec rule, never from running the runtime;
            - every check has a mutant it kills;
            - the null runtime fails every case;
            - runs are deterministic from a seed;
            - the verdict format and the old-suite comparison.

            The README keeps the how-to.

            - **May change:** the new Spec, the README.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a Spec restating the code's current behaviour → caught by
              skill:check-spec by an agent that did not write it.
            - **Gates:** `workflow check`.
            - **User's read:** the Spec's guarantees.
        acceptance
            The Spec exists, `workflow check` passes, and an independent skill:check-spec finds
            no gap in its contract.
    T5
        title       Suite renamed to Spec areas and behaviour names
        status      done
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T4]
        description
            One folder per core Spec (`write-lanes/`, ...), checks named by behaviour
            (`three-channels` to `ending-channels`, `one-delivery` to `delivered-once`, `lane-cells`
            to `lane-queue`), `*.lies.ts` to `*.mutants.ts` and "lie" to "mutant", scenario files by
            behaviour with the old `PAY-nn` id kept as a field, prototype leftovers renamed (README
            item 8). Blocked by T4, whose Spec settles the grouping.

            - **May change:** `packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/`.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a rename that drops or changes a check → caught by byte-identical
              suite, null and falsify output before and after.
            - **Gates:** falsify; `nub run check`.
        acceptance
            Suite, null and falsify output byte-identical before and after; `nub run check` at
            zero errors and warnings.
    T6
        title       Judged Runtime disposal per case, and tsgo in check
        status      done
        priority    medium
        blocked_by  [@T5]
        description
            Judge Runtime disposal at every case's end with the `disposal` oracle, and run `@effect/tsgo` in
            `nub run check`.

            **Why now:** round 5 dropped the implicit per-case disposal, so no case's end is judged, and the
            Effect language service does not run on TypeScript 7. It serves the phase goal (one oracle per
            guarantee) and @task.V3.T9, which shares the oracle.

            **Read first:** @spec.Actors.I29 to @spec.Actors.I32;
            conformance/README.md (item 9 of "The rest of the rewrite");
            conformance/actors/runtime-disposal.scenarios.ts#runtimeDisposalScenarios.
            The mutants: `lie.boot-says-disposed` and `lie.boot-drops-held` in
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/prototypes/conformance/falsify.ts, `o6.*` in
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/prototypes/round-14/mutants-lifetime.ts.

            - **May change:** `packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/`, `package.json`, the lint
              configuration.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a disposal oracle that never fails → caught by its mutants
              (`lie.boot-says-disposed`, `lie.boot-drops-held`, `o6.*`).
            - **Gates:** falsify; `nub run check`.
        acceptance
            - Every case ends with a judged disposal;
            - the disposal mutants are killed;
            - the tsgo language service runs in `nub run check`, which stays at zero.
    T40
        title       Suite simplified: one oracle contract, shared domain facts, dead surface removed
        status      done
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T6]
        description
            The suite's oracles share one step-fold contract and one definition of each domain fact, and its
            dead and copied code is gone, with every guarantee still judged.

            **Why now:** the simplicity review found an Attempt's life modelled five times, lane identity three
            ways, may-have-applied three ways, the Pay helpers copied into nine files, and every oracle
            re-folding the whole timeline each step. The remaining areas (T7 to T14) would copy that shape, and
            T7 rewrites two oracles that need the new contract first.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/suite-simplicity-review-2026-11-10.md
            (S1, S3 to S8, the patterns, and "Showing nothing got weaker"); @spec.Conformance;
            conformance/dsl/oracle.ts;
            conformance/actors/disposal.ts (its ledger, `disposal-ledger.ts`, was
            deleted at T7's step 6).

            **Approach:** in order, each landing alone with its gate: S5's attemptKey, write lookup and LaneId;
            S1 as a mechanical move, step bodies unchanged; S3, S4, S6, S7, and S8's runner items (not the adapter
            decode-once); S5's mayHaveApplied last, checked against WriteLanes R5, with any changed verdict listed
            with its rule. Share the pattern, not the state: no shared Attempt model. S2 (the rewrite of
            `lane-queue` and `delivered-once`) is @task.V3.T7's.

            - **May change:** `packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/` outside the two oracles T7 rewrites;
              `tools/lint-bomb/STYLE.md` for the review's two lines.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a simplification that drops a check while verdicts look the same → caught by the
              falsify sweep's red and caught-by sets compared before and after.
            - **Gates:** suite, null and falsify sweep byte-identical for verdict-neutral items; per-case verdict
              kind, oracle and Invariant for S1; `nub run check`.
            - **Stops:** a guarantee change.
        acceptance
            - Every oracle implements one step-fold contract with typed violations and InvariantId guarantees;
            - attemptKey, the write lookup, LaneId and mayHaveApplied each have one definition;
            - the Pay helpers live in one module; the dead surface the review lists is gone;
            - suite, null and falsify sweep outputs match before and after, except S5 mayHaveApplied changes
              listed with their rules;
            - `nub run check` at zero.
    T41
        title       Coverage gate: every core Invariant checked or owned
        status      done
        priority    high
        description
            A fast gate fails unless every Invariant in the core Specs has an oracle claiming it with a mutant
            caught by that Invariant, or an explicit "not yet" row naming the Task that owns it.

            **Why now:** falsify tests only what an oracle claims, so an Invariant with no oracle passes
            silently (I16 and I22 hid this way) until T15's coverage record.

            **Read first:** @spec.Conformance (R6, R12, I38); the guarantee map in
            conformance/README.md; `Mutant.expects` in
            conformance/dsl/oracle.ts.

            **Approach:** read Invariant ids from the core Specs (`workflow` CLI or the spec index), compare them
            with oracle `guarantee` lists, the falsify per-Invariant kills and a typed "not yet" table, and run it
            in the fast gates. Prove it with a planted uncovered Invariant that makes it fail.

            - **May change:** `packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/`, `package.json` scripts.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a "not yet" row that never expires → caught by T15's audit, which reads the table.
            - **Gates:** the planted uncovered Invariant; `nub run check`.
        acceptance
            - The gate lists every core Invariant as covered (oracle plus caught mutant) or "not yet" with an
              owning Task, and fails on any other;
            - a planted uncovered Invariant makes it fail;
            - it runs with the suite's fast gates.
    T42
        title       Core Specs revised from the Invariant audit and the open rulings
        status      done
        priority    high
        description
            The core Specs hold no conflicting Invariants or rules, carry the orchestrator's rulings, and drop or
            reword the audit's cut and untestable Invariants.

            **Why now:** the audit found 26 conflicts (21 new) that T7 to T12 and T17 would otherwise build against,
            and rulings M5, CQ1 to CQ7, Compile Q3, R9 and the retry Invariant are not yet in the Specs.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/invariant-audit-2026-11-11.md; the rulings
            in code:wiki/tasks/V3/log.task (2026-11-11); skill:to-spec.

            - **May change:** `wiki/specs/`, `packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/not-yet.ts` and coverage rows
              for cut or renumbered Invariants.
            - **Evidence:** spec-log.md entries; this Task's comment.
            - **Stops:** a ruling that would change a Plan's outcome goes to @plan.Pending.
        acceptance
            - C1 to C26 each resolved in the Specs or recorded with a reason;
            - the rulings and the gaps' new Invariants written; the 18 cuts and 7 rewordings applied;
            - `workflow check` valid and the coverage gate at 0 gaps.
